{
 "id": "NeverSleepC01",
 "slug": "never-sleep/c01",
 "chapter": "Hour zero",
 "topic": "What if you never slept again?",
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "p1",
   "text": "It's three a.m. Your whole house is asleep. Your mum. Your little sister Ellie. Even the cat."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p2",
   "text": "Everyone except you."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p3",
   "text": "Because last night, something switched off inside your head. You lay down, closed your eyes, and nothing happened. No yawn. No heavy eyelids. Nothing."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p4",
   "text": "You're not tired. And you won't be. Not tonight, not tomorrow, not ever again."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p5",
   "text": "At first, it sounds like a superpower. Eight free hours, every single night. Homework done by midnight. A new hobby by two. Breakfast for the whole family by six."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p6",
   "text": "But your body keeps its own clock. By hour nineteen, your brain works like it's had a few drinks. By day three, the shadows in the hallway start to move. And by day eleven, you'll be chasing a world record that nobody is even allowed to attempt anymore."
  },
  {
   "beat": "p7",
   "text": "So what really happens, hour by hour, if you never sleep again?"
  }
 ],
